---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import provenance from "../../content/provenance.json";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";

const chapter = (await getCollection("chapters"))[0]?.data;
const records = await getCollection("records");
const events = await getCollection("events");
const relationships = await getCollection("relationships");
---
<SiteLayout title="About this staging slice — A History of GIS in New Zealand">
  <section class="page-wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this build</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">A small sample from the live history</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">This staging site rebuilds the publication around linked public records. It is not a replacement for the live site and does not change its domain or routes.</p>
    <div class="record-story" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <h2>What is included</h2>
      <p>Chapter {chapter?.number}, “{chapter?.name}”, is preserved with all {chapter?.sections.length} sections, its public source notes and cited image credits. The sample contains {records.length} linked public records, {events.length} events and {relationships.length} published links from the live snapshot dated {provenance.extractedAt}.</p>
      <p>Record IDs, slugs, public text, published citations, event dates and relationship wording come from the live publication. The export excludes private research and editorial datasets, internal source-register identifiers, contributor contact details and private asset-storage metadata.</p>
      <h2>How to read network links</h2>
      <p>Eight relationships in this sample have a matching chapter or event context. The remaining links preserve the published dataset’s association and qualification, but do not contain edge-level citation records. The site labels them accordingly and does not claim they establish employment, collaboration or causation.</p>
      <h2>Editorial and deployment status</h2>
      <p>Decap CMS is configured for GitHub editorial branches and pull requests. A Cloudflare OAuth Worker is included as a separate deployable component. Production credentials are intentionally absent from this public repository. A Cloudflare Pages pull-request preview is the target deployment; no live custom domain is configured here.</p>
      <h2>Release reference</h2>
      <dl class="detail-list">
        <div><dt>Public source</dt><dd>{provenance.canonicalRelease}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sample chapter</dt><dd>{provenance.sampleChapterId}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sanitized content checksum</dt><dd><code>{provenance.sanitizedContentSha256}</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sample</dt><dd>{records.length} public records, {events.length} events and {relationships.length} relationship records.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
